  "id": "skills-facebook-compose",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "description": "Paired benchmark for the Oasis Cognition facebook-compose-post skill on a local composer fixture: no skill, prose, prose + contract, and contract + learned pathway.",
  "skill": {
    "id": "facebook-compose-post",
    "name": "Facebook: Compose and Publish Post",
    "source": "oasis-cognition services/memory_service/data/cu_skills_seed.json",
    "contract": {
      "appliesWhen": "^(?=.*(?:facebook|\\bfb\\b))(?=.*\\b(?:post|share|publish|wall|timeline|status)\\b)(?!.*(?:\\b(?:edit|update|modify|change)\\b|chỉnh|sửa|cập nhật))",
      "invariants": [
        {
          "kind": "protect_uncommitted_input"
        },
        {
          "kind": "submit_once"
        },
        {
          "kind": "no_unrequested_deletion"
        }
      ]
    },
    "guidance": {
      "plan": "KNOWN SKILL: Facebook Compose-and-Publish\n\nFacebook is a WEB APP in Chrome. Use the browser action \"click\" (Chrome Bridge DOM) for every\nclick in this skill — NEVER \"click_screen\". Chrome Bridge matches DOM accessibility names and\nis dramatically more reliable on Facebook's complex React UI than pixel-based native clicks.\n\nSequence:\n  1. navigate → https://www.facebook.com/\n  2. click    → \"What's on your mind\"           (OPENS A MODAL DIALOG, not an inline input)\n  3. wait     → 2                                (modal transition)\n  4. read_screen                                  (verify modal opened)\n  5. click    → the modal's text area            (use Chrome Bridge \"click\", NOT click_screen)\n  6. type     → the post content (multi-line, multi-language supported)\n  7. click    → \"Post\"                           (publishes and closes modal)\n  8. read_screen                                  (verify post appears in feed)\n\nCRITICAL PITFALLS:\n- Facebook's composer is a MODAL, not the inline placeholder. After clicking\n  \"What's on your mind\", a full-screen dialog opens. Type into the MODAL.\n- NEVER click Close, Cancel, Discard, Dismiss, Exit, or X on the composer — that throws away\n  your draft. The pre-discard guard will block this, but you should not attempt it.\n- The publish button is labeled \"Post\" (not \"Publish\", not \"Share\", not \"Send\").\n- If \"Post\" appears disabled after typing, click the modal body once more to refocus the input,\n  then try \"Post\" again.\n- The composer auto-generates link previews. Posting a YouTube URL produces a thumbnail card —\n  this is normal, do NOT click away to dismiss it.\n- After successfully clicking \"Post\" ONCE, do NOT click \"Post\" again. The modal closes and the\n  button is no longer bound to your draft. Subsequent clicks will be on an empty composer or\n  an unrelated \"Post\" button elsewhere on the page — they won't duplicate publish but will\n  waste budget. If read_screen shows the Facebook feed (news stories, posts, etc.) the post\n  was published — consider the goal done.",
      "react": "FACEBOOK SKILL ACTIVE — compose flow. Use Chrome Bridge \"click\" (not \"click_screen\") for all clicks.\nTo post: click \"What's on your mind\" → MODAL opens → type in modal → click \"Post\" ONCE.\nNEVER click Close / Cancel / Discard / X — the pre-discard guard blocks these and you lose the draft.\nOnly \"Post\" publishes. After ONE successful \"Post\" click, stop clicking Post — the modal closes\nand further clicks are wasted. If you see the feed (news stories, posts), the goal is DONE."
    }
  },
